WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.203
Welcome back.

00:00:01.203 --> 00:00:09.882
This video is about Long-term rooms: a private room you can keep using with the same person, for up to thirty days at a time.

00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:13.770
We will also walk through every setting inside the room.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.598
Which one should you pick?

00:00:16.598 --> 00:00:23.488
A Temp room is deleted thirty minutes after you both leave, and is best for a quick, private talk.

00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:31.715
A Long-term room stays until nobody has been inside it for thirty days, and every visit starts the thirty days again.

00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:35.160
It is best for a conversation you will return to.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.851
On the Create tab, choose Long term.

00:00:38.851 --> 00:00:48.346
The note explains it: the room stays until nobody has been in it for thirty days, and every visit starts the thirty days again.

00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:50.140
Then tap Create my room.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:57.491
You get the same three items as before: the room key, your Pass Code and your partner’s Pass Code.

00:00:57.491 --> 00:01:01.898
The room is labelled Long-term, so you always know which type it is.

00:01:01.898 --> 00:01:05.008
Copy them now, because they are shown only once.

00:01:05.008 --> 00:01:09.480
Keep them somewhere safe, since this room will be around for a while.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.153
About the secret phrase.

00:01:12.153 --> 00:01:21.218
With a phrase, your partner must type it to get in, and the key exists only on your two devices, so not even we can read the chat.

00:01:21.218 --> 00:01:24.216
If it is forgotten, it cannot be recovered.

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:27.632
Without a phrase, your partner walks straight in.

00:01:27.632 --> 00:01:33.838
Messages are still encrypted, but the key comes from the room key, which our server sees.

00:01:33.838 --> 00:01:38.300
So for a room you will keep for weeks, we do recommend a phrase.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.630
A room without a phrase shows an amber lock at the top, so both of you always know.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.520
Tap or hover over it to read the explanation.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.755
Now the settings.

00:01:49.755 --> 00:01:52.226
Everything lives in Room settings.

00:01:52.226 --> 00:01:55.860
Open it with the sliders button, at the top right.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.066
At the top, choose a nickname.

00:01:59.066 --> 00:02:02.374
Your partner sees it instead of Your partner.

00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:06.417
Below that, pick an emoji and a colour as your picture.

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:11.490
Both are encrypted like your messages, and no photo is ever uploaded.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:19.375
Disappearing messages lets you choose off, thirty seconds, five minutes, one hour, or twenty four hours.

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:25.400
New messages then vanish for both of you after that time, counted from when they were sent.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:33.056
Under Privacy, Blur when I look away hides the chat as soon as you switch to another tab or app.

00:02:33.056 --> 00:02:35.968
Sounds plays a soft tone for new messages.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:43.941
And Auto sign-out ends your session after a period with no activity, so someone passing by cannot read your screen.

00:02:43.941 --> 00:02:46.090
You will need your codes again.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.472
Hide now closes the chat instantly.

00:02:49.472 --> 00:02:52.875
On a computer, you can press the Escape key twice.

00:02:52.875 --> 00:02:55.870
Use it whenever someone walks up behind you.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:02.965
Under Conversation, Clear chat for both erases every message, for you and your partner.

00:03:02.965 --> 00:03:04.366
It cannot be undone.

00:03:04.366 --> 00:03:09.550
Leave the room signs you out, but the room itself stays, until it expires.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.430
Vanish mode is the ghost button in the header.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:16.999
It is off by default, and either of you can switch it on.

00:03:16.999 --> 00:03:21.320
When it is on, a banner reminds you that new messages will disappear.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.365
The countdown starts the moment your partner sees a message.

00:03:26.365 --> 00:03:32.567
You both see the numbers, the message fades, and then it is erased, from our server as well.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.937
Messages that were not yet seen are never removed.

00:03:35.937 --> 00:03:39.780
Messages sent before you switched it on are not affected.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.880
Two more tools.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:48.773
View once, with the dotted circle button, sends a message your partner can open only one time.

00:03:48.773 --> 00:03:55.300
And to take back something you sent, open the menu of your own message and choose Unsend.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.500
It is removed for both of you.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.516
To keep a Long-term room alive, just visit now and then.

00:04:02.516 --> 00:04:05.097
Each visit restarts the thirty days.

00:04:05.097 --> 00:04:12.340
If nobody enters for thirty days, the room is deleted, with every message, and it cannot be restored.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:16.227
Do use a phrase for a room you will keep.

00:04:16.227 --> 00:04:20.382
Do store your codes safely, since they are shown only once.

00:04:20.382 --> 00:04:25.663
Do use Hide now when someone is near, and do visit before thirty days pass.

00:04:25.663 --> 00:04:28.831
Do not treat it as a backup of your messages.

00:04:28.831 --> 00:04:31.578
Never share the phrase next to the key.

00:04:31.578 --> 00:04:33.760
Lost codes cannot be recovered.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.070
And do not stay signed in on a shared computer.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:41.403
That is the Long-term room, and all its settings.

00:04:41.403 --> 00:04:45.280
Create yours at one two one dot the secret basket dot in.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.226
Next, watch the Random video, to meet someone new, safely.

00:04:49.226 --> 00:04:50.790
Thank you for watching.
